WEBVTT

00:00:53.810 --> 00:01:04.349
Northeast sector. Contact.

00:01:04.349 --> 00:01:05.349
Tony seven.

00:01:05.349 --> 00:01:14.420
Lock it down.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:42.549
It's such a good idea.

00:01:42.549 --> 00:02:16.780
Back for further instructions.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:19.780
Biden's a steady.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.780
He didn't even break a sweat.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.780
Two minutes, 18 seconds to infiltrate a secured facility.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:28.780
Disable my best manner and eliminate the target.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.780
Not a bad test run.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:35.120
Get some fresh guards.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:03:40.639
I want to see him do it again.

00:03:40.639 --> 00:03:43.639
We have about a dozen people that could do that for you.

00:03:43.639 --> 00:03:46.639
The next thing you know, they'll be brushing my teeth for me.

00:03:46.639 --> 00:03:49.639
There are some things I'd rather do on my own.

00:03:49.639 --> 00:03:53.979
Independent and not afraid to get her hands dirty.

00:03:53.979 --> 00:03:56.979
Two of the billion or so reasons I fell in love with you.

00:03:56.979 --> 00:04:02.379
The shoulders are still a little bit sore.

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:04.379
Maybe we should have the doctor look at it again.

00:04:04.379 --> 00:04:06.379
No, it's okay.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:08.379
Lana, you were showing.

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:11.379
It takes more than a bullet to stop Eluther.

00:04:11.379 --> 00:04:20.579
Sir, Senator Burke has arrived.

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:22.579
Show him in.

00:04:22.579 --> 00:04:23.579
You've been seeing a lot of this at.

00:04:23.579 --> 00:04:25.579
I've been seeing a lot of the senator recently.

00:04:25.579 --> 00:04:27.579
The price of doing business with the government.

00:04:27.579 --> 00:04:29.579
Look, this will just take a minute.

00:04:29.579 --> 00:04:34.300
I'll be in the garden.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.300
Mrs. Luther?

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.300
Senator.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:40.300
I hope I didn't interrupt the tender moment.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.300
If you had, you'd still be waiting outside.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.300
I'm not going to keep you from your pretty lady.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.300
I just, uh...

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.300
so on by for an update on Aries.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.300
Prototype is in the final stages of testing.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.300
Everything's on schedule.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.300
Really?

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:59.300
I heard everything it was ahead of schedule.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.300
Way ahead.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.300
I stuck my neck out to get the Armed Services Committee

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.300
to allow you access to military resources and personnel

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.300
to R&D's single prototype,

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:13.300
but you've started gearing up for mass production.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:16.300
Just looking towards the future, Senator.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:20.300
I assumed a visionary like you would understand that.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.300
How long do you think you're going to be able to keep

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.300
what you really got going on here is secret?

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.300
a secret. See?

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.300
One of my own men.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.300
He believed he uncovered a mole right in your backyard.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.029
Who?

00:05:35.029 --> 00:05:39.029
Well, I wish I could tell you, but my boy doesn't talk too good

00:05:39.029 --> 00:05:42.029
with a bullet through his heart.

00:05:42.029 --> 00:05:45.029
Senator, if there are leaks in my security,

00:05:45.029 --> 00:05:47.029
I assure you I will have them taken care of.

00:05:47.029 --> 00:05:51.029
Well, doesn't that just fill me with the warm fuzzies?

00:05:51.029 --> 00:05:55.029
Do you know what'll happen to me if the Senate ever got wind of what you're up to now?

00:05:55.029 --> 00:05:58.029
I assume they wouldn't care for it.

00:05:58.029 --> 00:06:01.029
Just like they wouldn't care for all the money I've transferred

00:06:01.029 --> 00:06:04.029
and your Cayman account over the last year.

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:07.029
Project Aries is over.

00:06:07.029 --> 00:06:09.029
I'm shutting it down.

00:06:09.029 --> 00:06:16.319
That would be ill-advised.

00:06:16.319 --> 00:06:17.319
It's ill-advised.

00:06:17.319 --> 00:06:20.319
Is you ever opening your mouth about our arrangement?

00:06:20.319 --> 00:06:22.319
I, so much as you're a peep out of you,

00:06:22.319 --> 00:06:25.319
I'll make sure the committee reviews every business deal

00:06:25.319 --> 00:06:27.319
that the Luthorpe has made in the last 20 years.

00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:29.319
You'll be lucky to keep that.

00:06:29.319 --> 00:06:31.319
fancy shirt on your back.

00:06:31.319 --> 00:06:34.319
We understand each other?

00:06:34.319 --> 00:06:35.319
Luther.

00:06:35.319 --> 00:07:47.709
We have to talk.

00:07:47.709 --> 00:07:55.029
You should try picking up a phone occasionally.

00:07:55.029 --> 00:07:56.029
Might be quicker.

00:07:56.029 --> 00:07:58.029
Maybe not.

00:07:58.029 --> 00:08:00.029
What do you know about Lana?

00:08:00.029 --> 00:08:03.470
Uh, letting go.

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:08.139
Never been one of your strong points, was it?

00:08:08.139 --> 00:08:10.139
Telling the truth is never one of yours.

00:08:10.139 --> 00:08:13.420
And you're accusing me of...

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.420
What, exactly?

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:16.420
This time.

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:20.269
Lana came to me the day of the wedding

00:08:20.269 --> 00:08:21.269
to tell me she wasn't going.

00:08:21.269 --> 00:08:23.269
going through with it.

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:26.839
That she was leaving Lex.

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:27.839
Apparently she changed her mind.

00:08:27.839 --> 00:08:29.839
Or someone changed it for her.

00:08:29.839 --> 00:08:37.129
So you think I had something to do with her decision?

00:08:37.129 --> 00:08:40.129
Lana was so unhappy with Lex, why I got through with the marriage?

00:08:40.129 --> 00:08:44.129
It's surprising, Clark, what people will do when they, uh,

00:08:44.129 --> 00:08:46.129
feel they have no other options.

00:08:46.129 --> 00:08:53.870
If I find out that you had anything to do with Lana marrying Lex,

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:58.500
the gloves will come off.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:12.570
How do you like that option?

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.570
espresso moka capu latte,

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.570
my own invention, guaranteed to put the zimpy back in your duda.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:18.570
Thanks.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:21.230
Come on.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:24.230
It's not that bad. Jimmy is coming back.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:25.230
One day.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.230
Maybe.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:30.230
You know, besides, distance is good for the relationship.

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:33.230
That is what all the guys who've moved away from me have said.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:36.230
Lois, you should really stick to investigative reporting

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:38.230
and out of the advice call.

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:40.230
That's the plan.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:45.370
Hey, Smallville.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:50.370
Love to hear about the cows on the corn, but I got a lead on a dirty senator that needs to be hosed down.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:51.370
See you on the front page.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.370
She's going after a senator?

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:56.370
I guess so. She hasn't told me much about it.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:10:00.100
A lot of that going around lately.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:02.100
Was that jab directed at my chin?

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:05.820
Delano, I'll ask about Lana.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:06.820
What did he say?

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:08.820
Nothing. Just like you.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.330
Clark, I...

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:13.330
Oh, you know what Lex is really like.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:17.330
Did you forget what he did to you, what he did to your mother?

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:19.330
No, I haven't forgotten.

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:22.659
I don't.

00:10:22.659 --> 00:10:24.659
I don't want anything to happen to Lana.

00:10:24.659 --> 00:10:25.659
Neither do I.

00:10:25.659 --> 00:10:27.659
But if she's staying in that marriage,

00:10:27.659 --> 00:10:29.659
all I can say is she must have a damn good reason.

00:10:29.659 --> 00:10:40.690
You sure about this?

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:42.690
Got a reservation.

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:44.690
It's here every time he's in town.

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:46.690
Walla.

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:48.690
Thanks for the tip.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:56.019
Senator Burke.

00:10:56.019 --> 00:10:57.019
Hi to this.

00:10:57.019 --> 00:10:59.019
Lois Lane, reporter.

00:10:59.019 --> 00:11:01.019
I was hoping to ask a few questions.

00:11:01.019 --> 00:11:03.019
Sure, schedule an interview with my office.

00:11:03.019 --> 00:11:07.019
You know, I try to, but no one returned my calls.

00:11:07.019 --> 00:11:11.019
Well, that ought to tell you some sweet cakes.

00:11:11.019 --> 00:11:17.740
Senator, last year your salary was $150,000.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:27.700
Can you tell me how you managed to deposit over $5 million in a Cayman account?

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.700
What paper did you say you work for?

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:32.700
Lane. Lois Lane.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:34.700
I'm a reporter for The Inquisitor.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.700
The Inquisitor?

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:38.700
That's not a newspaper.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:41.700
That's a... that's a cat box liner.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.700
Get her out of here.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.700
Hey, get your hands off with you, you fast!

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:47.700
Not warning you!

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:48.700
You don't...

00:11:48.700 --> 00:12:17.129
What?

00:12:17.129 --> 00:12:41.679
Lowe, what's going on?

00:12:41.679 --> 00:12:42.679
You haven't heard?

00:12:42.679 --> 00:12:43.679
Senator Burke was murdered.

00:12:43.679 --> 00:12:44.679
What?

00:12:44.679 --> 00:12:46.679
Yeah, it looks like Burke was in bed with La Familia.

00:12:46.679 --> 00:12:47.679
He crossed them.

00:12:47.679 --> 00:12:48.679
They gave him the Fredo treatment.

00:12:48.679 --> 00:12:49.679
His mom head.

00:12:49.679 --> 00:12:51.679
Well, all evidence points to that,

00:12:51.679 --> 00:12:53.679
but there is one witness who doesn't think so.

00:12:53.679 --> 00:12:54.679
Lois?

00:12:54.679 --> 00:13:02.700
What happened to you?

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:06.700
Uh, well, one minute I was harassing a public official,

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:07.700
and the next...

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:10.700
He came out of nowhere, like a ghost.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:11.700
Burk and his...

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:13.700
This man never had a chance.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:15.700
You saw who did this?

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.700
Yeah, I did more than see him, Clark. I know him.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:22.700
His name is Wes Keenan. We were Army brats together and we were kids.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:24.700
I'm running a check on his name.

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:29.220
Looks like he works for the mob now.

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:32.220
Wes? No way.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:35.220
He's career military. He's been decorated more than a Christmas treat.

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:38.220
Even my dad loved him. And the general hates everybody.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:41.220
Lois, are you sure the man you saw is West Keenan?

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.220
I haven't seen him for years, but he has this little scar above his right-up.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:45.220
scar above his right eye and...

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:48.220
Trust me. It was Wes.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:51.220
Not according to the U.S. government.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:54.220
He was in a helicopter crash in Afghanistan four months ago.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.220
He was killed in action.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:14:02.259
That is not possible. I know what I saw.

00:14:02.259 --> 00:14:05.960
What else does it say?

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:06.960
Nothing.

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:09.960
I mean, his military records have been classified.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:22.000
What is that?

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.000
As alpha wave just spiked for a second.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:28.000
It's probably just feedback from the implants in his cortex.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:29.000
Probably.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.000
It's nothing to worry about.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.000
Everything's still holding within operational parameters.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.000
Make sure it stays that way.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:43.870
We just received information that Burke has been eliminated.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:44.870
Evidence trial?

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:47.870
Lead straight back to the mob for your instructions.

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:49.870
There's been a complication.

00:14:51.889 --> 00:14:52.889
It was a witness.

00:14:52.889 --> 00:14:54.889
Nothing.

00:14:54.889 --> 00:14:57.889
King Gate in the way of completing this project.

00:14:57.889 --> 00:15:02.769
Nothing.

00:15:02.769 --> 00:15:03.769
Take care of it.

00:15:03.769 --> 00:15:09.860
You heard the man.

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:10.860
Prep him.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:28.059
Let us, quit being stubborn.

00:15:28.059 --> 00:15:31.059
You're going to stay here until we get this cleared up.

00:15:31.059 --> 00:15:34.059
Thanks, but I can take care of myself.

00:15:34.059 --> 00:15:37.059
Nobody's dying now, but I think you'd be safer here at the farm.

00:15:37.059 --> 00:15:38.059
It would be like old times.

00:15:38.059 --> 00:15:40.059
Like when you first got to small go.

00:15:40.059 --> 00:15:42.059
Oh, you're just hoping to catch me in the shower again.

00:15:42.059 --> 00:15:46.940
I mean, um, thank you.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.940
I really appreciate it.

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:50.940
Well, you're always welcome here, Lois.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:52.940
You're practically family.

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:57.940
Uh, well, since I'm being a burden, can I just ask one more favor?

00:15:57.940 --> 00:15:58.940
favor.

00:15:58.940 --> 00:15:59.940
What do you need?

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:03.799
Your mom's political influence.

00:16:03.799 --> 00:16:13.279
Look, do you think that you could use your connections to get a look at Wes's military jacket?

00:16:13.279 --> 00:16:15.279
I thought you said the file was classified.

00:16:15.279 --> 00:16:17.279
It is.

00:16:17.279 --> 00:16:21.279
I contacted the general, but he went all cold war on me and said that I should drop it.

00:16:21.279 --> 00:16:23.279
Well, he might have a point.

00:16:23.279 --> 00:16:25.279
Three men are already dead.

00:16:25.279 --> 00:16:28.279
Which is why I have to get my hands on that file.

00:16:28.279 --> 00:16:31.279
It might explain why Wes is doing this.

00:16:31.279 --> 00:16:35.620
I've made a few friends in Washington.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:40.620
I don't know if they can help, but I'll see what I can do.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:45.750
Thanks, Mrs. Kay.

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:46.750
I know that, look.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:49.750
And it's usually followed by you almost getting yourself killed.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:51.750
Well, this isn't just another story, Clark.

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:53.750
Not this time.

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:56.750
Wes and I, we were close.

00:16:56.750 --> 00:17:02.080
I know it was him.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.080
Stay here.

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:18.009
Looks like it was just the wind.

00:17:18.009 --> 00:17:47.589
How could Lois have been kidnapped with you standing right there?

00:17:47.589 --> 00:17:49.589
She just vanished, Chloe, literally.

00:17:49.589 --> 00:17:51.589
So he could teleport like Alicia?

00:17:51.589 --> 00:17:52.589
Alicia?

00:17:52.589 --> 00:17:53.589
That's time it was different.

00:17:53.589 --> 00:17:54.589
It was more like Graham Garrett could do.

00:17:54.589 --> 00:17:56.589
So he could turn himself invisible?

00:17:56.589 --> 00:17:57.589
Not just himself.

00:17:57.589 --> 00:17:58.589
He took Lois with him.

00:17:58.589 --> 00:18:00.589
And it's not his only ability.

00:18:00.589 --> 00:18:04.589
And when he hit me, Chloe, I haven't felt anything like that

00:18:04.589 --> 00:18:07.589
since I went up against Titan.

00:18:07.589 --> 00:18:09.589
Clark, we need to find Lois before Wes.

00:18:09.589 --> 00:18:10.589
We will.

00:18:10.589 --> 00:18:14.589
Were you able uncover anything about Wes that might be able to help us figure out where

00:18:14.589 --> 00:18:15.589
he took her?

00:18:15.589 --> 00:18:18.589
I haven't been able to retrieve any information from the military files.

00:18:18.589 --> 00:18:20.589
But I did run a cross-check on his name.

00:18:20.589 --> 00:18:23.589
check on his name and I found one hit, Jody Keenan.

00:18:23.589 --> 00:18:24.589
Jody Keenan?

00:18:24.589 --> 00:18:25.589
Jody Keenan.

00:18:25.589 --> 00:18:27.589
Isn't that the woman who tried to kill Lex in the tunnels?

00:18:27.589 --> 00:18:29.589
Guess who she's married to.

00:18:29.589 --> 00:18:30.589
Wes?

00:18:30.589 --> 00:18:33.589
Looks like Jody found out that Wes wasn't killed in Afghanistan.

00:18:33.589 --> 00:18:36.589
And she followed the trail all the way back here to Lex.

00:18:36.589 --> 00:18:38.589
Okay.

00:18:38.589 --> 00:18:41.589
So Wes is exhibiting multiple crypto abilities and according to Lois,

00:18:41.589 --> 00:18:45.589
he's also on the receiving end of some sort of mind control.

00:18:45.589 --> 00:18:49.589
How much do you want to bet that all of this plays into Lex's 33.1 experiments?

00:18:49.589 --> 00:18:50.589
one experiments.

00:18:50.589 --> 00:18:52.589
Chloe, I need you to contact Oliver and his team.

00:18:52.589 --> 00:18:55.589
They've been taking out 33.1 facilities all around the world.

00:18:55.589 --> 00:18:57.589
Don't you think that's a hero to hero phone call?

00:18:57.589 --> 00:18:59.589
I'm going to talk to Lex.

00:18:59.589 --> 00:19:00.589
Clerk, come on.

00:19:00.589 --> 00:19:02.589
We both know that Lex isn't going to tell you anything.

00:19:02.589 --> 00:19:06.609
And I'll find somebody who will.

00:19:06.609 --> 00:19:25.240
Too much?

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:27.240
No.

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:33.069
It's...

00:19:33.069 --> 00:19:55.609
Maybe if I set the mood.

00:19:55.609 --> 00:19:56.609
Sorry to bother you, sir.

00:19:56.609 --> 00:20:01.519
The asset failed to return.

00:20:01.519 --> 00:20:25.019
I'll be right back.

00:20:25.019 --> 00:20:27.019
You shouldn't be here. Lex is just outside.

00:20:27.019 --> 00:20:28.019
I had to see you.

00:20:28.019 --> 00:20:33.920
It's not about you and me.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.920
me. Lois is in trouble.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.920
And what makes you think I can help?

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:40.920
Because it seems just a connection to Lex.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:46.920
Lana, if you've seen or heard anything, maybe something about the military?

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:49.680
Aries.

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:54.880
It's the god of war.

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:59.880
Lex has been talking with Senator Burke about this military project called Aries.

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:04.450
Yesterday, he threatened to shut it down.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:07.819
Maybe you should talk with him.

00:21:07.819 --> 00:21:09.819
Senator Burke is dead.

00:21:09.819 --> 00:21:11.819
He was murdered by the same man who has Lois.

00:21:11.819 --> 00:21:12.819
As Lois.

00:21:12.819 --> 00:21:16.609
Lana, is there anything else?

00:21:16.609 --> 00:21:19.609
Maybe something that Lex let slip.

00:21:19.609 --> 00:21:24.609
One of his men was just saying something about an asset that failed to return.

00:21:24.609 --> 00:21:28.880
An asset?

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:34.309
That's what the military calls it soldiers.

00:21:34.309 --> 00:21:38.579
Lex is connected to this.

00:21:38.579 --> 00:21:40.579
On whatever reason you had to go through at the wedding,

00:21:40.579 --> 00:21:41.579
it was the wrong choice.

00:21:41.579 --> 00:21:43.579
You have no idea what he's capable of.

00:21:43.579 --> 00:21:47.339
You'd be surprised what I know.

00:21:47.339 --> 00:21:57.119
Why, you're still here?

00:21:57.119 --> 00:22:00.750
We all have our secrets, Clark.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:27.220
Sometimes we have to keep them to protect the people that we care about.

00:22:27.220 --> 00:22:28.220
What?

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:31.039
You okay?

00:22:31.039 --> 00:22:34.039
Yeah. Yeah, I'm just a little chilly.

00:22:34.039 --> 00:22:42.829
Look, something's come up.

00:22:42.829 --> 00:22:44.829
I need to go into the office.

00:22:44.829 --> 00:23:44.569
Carlson and Harry's prototype, Mark 4.

00:23:44.569 --> 00:23:48.259
You don't remember me, do you?

00:23:48.259 --> 00:23:50.259
It's Lois.

00:23:50.259 --> 00:23:52.259
Lois Lane?

00:23:52.259 --> 00:23:55.259
My father is General Sam Lane.

00:23:55.259 --> 00:23:59.259
When I was a kid, he used to drag me around to all the bases that

00:23:59.259 --> 00:24:01.259
he was stationed at.

00:24:01.259 --> 00:24:05.259
One of them was Fort Avelson, where I met you.

00:24:05.259 --> 00:24:11.400
Do you remember how you got that scar?

00:24:11.400 --> 00:24:15.400
You used to tell everybody that you got it falling off your dirt bike.

00:24:15.400 --> 00:24:19.900
That's not how it happened.

00:24:19.900 --> 00:24:22.900
We got into the General's Whiskey.

00:24:22.900 --> 00:24:25.900
Then we broke into the storage warehouse.

00:24:25.900 --> 00:24:34.380
We were wrestling around being stupid, and I kissed you.

00:24:34.380 --> 00:24:36.380
The first time I ever kissed anybody.

00:24:36.380 --> 00:24:44.190
And you smiled your crooked smile, and then you

00:24:44.210 --> 00:24:47.210
Puked and passed out and cracked your head open on the floor.

00:24:47.210 --> 00:24:51.029
Ever could handle your liquor, Wes?

00:24:51.029 --> 00:25:00.799
Can you complete?

00:25:00.799 --> 00:25:02.799
Eliminate Target.

00:25:02.799 --> 00:25:07.740
Why did you bring me here?

00:25:07.740 --> 00:25:10.500
Wes?

00:25:10.500 --> 00:25:14.500
This is Fort Abelson, okay? This is the warehouse.

00:25:14.500 --> 00:25:49.309
This is where I kissed you that night.

00:25:49.309 --> 00:25:50.309
Mr. Luther.

00:25:50.309 --> 00:25:52.309
Three years and a billion dollars spent on Aries

00:25:52.309 --> 00:25:53.309
and you're telling me you lost him?

00:25:53.309 --> 00:25:56.309
We're in uncharted territory here, Mr. Luther.

00:25:56.309 --> 00:25:59.309
Synthesizing multiple meteor abilities is difficult enough,

00:25:59.309 --> 00:26:01.309
but stringing together the molecular chain.

00:26:01.309 --> 00:26:05.009
with peptides extracted from that creature that Bartlett recovered.

00:26:05.009 --> 00:26:09.309
The only thing that allows all these abilities to exist in one subject.

00:26:09.309 --> 00:26:12.309
Titan's genetic material was the key to making this project viable.

00:26:12.309 --> 00:26:17.309
Yes, which makes the results as unpredictable as the substances I'm being asked to work with.

00:26:17.309 --> 00:26:20.309
What you're being asked to do is help protect the world, Doctor.

00:26:20.309 --> 00:26:24.309
Unstable criminals with dangerous powers are becoming more and more common.

00:26:24.309 --> 00:26:29.309
Humanity's only chance to survive in the onslaught is this project.

00:26:29.309 --> 00:26:31.309
So kick that big brand of yours in high gear.

00:26:31.309 --> 00:26:33.309
and figure out what the hell went wrong.

00:26:33.309 --> 00:26:36.309
It's possible something might have triggered a decay in his memory blocks,

00:26:36.309 --> 00:26:38.309
a familiar place or person.

00:26:38.309 --> 00:26:40.309
Can't you get a fix on him?

00:26:40.309 --> 00:26:43.309
The field he generates makes it impossible to track him electronically.

00:26:43.309 --> 00:26:45.309
It's part of his design.

00:26:45.309 --> 00:26:47.309
I want our dog back on his leash, doctor.

00:26:47.309 --> 00:26:50.309
Or you'll be my next experiment.

00:26:50.309 --> 00:26:55.940
Maybe I could reposition the Luther Corp satellites.

00:26:55.940 --> 00:27:02.539
Generate a broad spectrum pulse that will hopefully reinitiate his command directives,

00:27:02.539 --> 00:27:03.539
but there's no guarantee.

00:27:03.539 --> 00:27:04.539
I'm not asking for guarantees.

00:27:04.539 --> 00:27:10.539
for guarantees. I'm asking for results. I want Aries back online and his mission completed.

00:27:10.539 --> 00:27:14.680
Start the pulse.

00:27:14.680 --> 00:27:38.180
I killed the United States Senator.

00:27:38.180 --> 00:27:42.259
What happened?

00:27:42.259 --> 00:27:44.259
How did you end up like this?

00:27:44.259 --> 00:27:53.180
I was stationed in Afghanistan.

00:27:53.180 --> 00:27:56.980
Our convoy hit an IAT.

00:27:56.980 --> 00:28:00.319
And then I woke up in the military hospital.

00:28:00.319 --> 00:28:04.180
That's when Luther showed up.

00:28:04.180 --> 00:28:05.180
Lex.

00:28:05.180 --> 00:28:09.190
He should have known.

00:28:09.190 --> 00:28:13.180
He forced you into this, didn't he?

00:28:13.180 --> 00:28:15.180
He offered me a way to keep serving my way to keep serving my

00:28:15.180 --> 00:28:16.180
country.

00:28:16.180 --> 00:28:18.180
By turning you into a brain-dead assassin?

00:28:18.180 --> 00:28:21.180
You think this is what I signed on for?

00:28:21.180 --> 00:28:25.180
He told me Project Arias was going to help soldiers protect themselves on the field,

00:28:25.180 --> 00:28:27.180
so they wouldn't end up like I did.

00:28:27.180 --> 00:28:30.180
We won't let him get away with this, I promise you.

00:28:30.180 --> 00:28:33.180
Okay, we will expose Lex and Project Aries.

00:28:33.180 --> 00:28:38.099
What is he?

00:28:38.099 --> 00:28:39.099
Wes?

00:28:39.099 --> 00:28:40.099
It's...

00:28:40.099 --> 00:28:42.099
I'm...

00:28:42.099 --> 00:28:45.099
Try to get back in my head.

00:28:45.099 --> 00:28:46.099
You'll find it, please look at me!

00:28:46.099 --> 00:28:47.099
Look at me!

00:28:47.099 --> 00:28:48.099
Look at me!

00:28:48.099 --> 00:28:49.099
Run!

00:28:49.099 --> 00:28:50.099
Run!

00:28:50.099 --> 00:29:13.430
Run!

00:29:13.430 --> 00:29:14.430
I think Lex was experimenting on Wes,

00:29:14.430 --> 00:29:16.430
trying to make him into a super soldier.

00:29:16.430 --> 00:29:19.430
With Pick and Choose Media Powers, Oliver told me pretty much the same thing.

00:29:19.430 --> 00:29:20.430
Oliver knew about Wes?

00:29:20.430 --> 00:29:21.430
No.

00:29:21.430 --> 00:29:23.430
He found an earlier model in the Utah desert.

00:29:23.430 --> 00:29:27.430
It looks like this isn't the first time one of Lex's souped-up Rambo's has gone to anal.

00:29:27.430 --> 00:29:28.430
Was he able to stop him?

00:29:28.430 --> 00:29:29.430
Barely.

00:29:29.430 --> 00:29:32.430
It took the equivalent of a mini- nuke to break through his force field.

00:29:32.430 --> 00:29:33.430
Clark, even if you find him...

00:29:33.430 --> 00:29:35.430
Maybe this will help.

00:29:35.430 --> 00:29:36.430
West's military jacket.

00:29:36.430 --> 00:29:38.430
How did you get that?

00:29:38.430 --> 00:29:39.430
Called in a few favors.

00:29:39.430 --> 00:29:41.430
I had to promise a couple dozen of my own.

00:29:41.430 --> 00:29:43.430
Lois is right. Wes was a hero.

00:29:43.430 --> 00:29:46.430
He took her instead of killing her.

00:29:46.430 --> 00:29:49.430
You know, if whatever programming they're using to control Wes is failing,

00:29:49.430 --> 00:29:51.430
maybe he'll go back to a place he remembers.

00:29:51.430 --> 00:29:54.430
Somewhere he lived or was stationed.

00:29:54.430 --> 00:29:59.480
The military base that Wes grew up on was decommissioned a few years ago.

00:29:59.480 --> 00:30:01.480
Fort Avelson just outside of Metropolis.

00:30:01.480 --> 00:30:04.480
Sam Lane was stationed there when Lois was in junior high.

00:30:04.480 --> 00:30:05.480
Maybe he was...

00:30:05.480 --> 00:30:11.119
Did you get used to that?

00:30:11.119 --> 00:30:43.200
Not really.

00:30:43.200 --> 00:30:46.470
Wes.

00:30:46.470 --> 00:30:47.470
You have to fight this.

00:30:47.470 --> 00:30:52.490
Don't let them do this to you again.

00:30:52.490 --> 00:30:56.150
You are not a murderer.

00:30:56.150 --> 00:30:58.779
Please.

00:30:58.779 --> 00:33:04.309
Wes, do you understand me? You're gonna be okay.

00:33:04.309 --> 00:33:06.309
I'm gonna go get out, alright?

00:33:06.309 --> 00:33:16.210
No. They'll never stop trying to control me.

00:33:16.210 --> 00:33:18.210
You have to stay with me.

00:33:18.210 --> 00:33:20.210
Do you hear me?

00:33:20.210 --> 00:33:21.210
Don't.

00:33:21.210 --> 00:33:33.619
I promise, but you just stay with me, okay? Don't leave me.

00:33:33.619 --> 00:34:18.210
All Wes wanted to do is service country,

00:34:18.210 --> 00:34:20.210
and you wound up being used as a pawn.

00:34:20.210 --> 00:34:21.210
It happens more than I like to think.

00:34:21.210 --> 00:34:23.210
think.

00:34:23.210 --> 00:34:25.210
Well, now that Senator Burke is gone.

00:34:25.210 --> 00:34:28.210
Burke isn't the only one on the hell lining his pockets.

00:34:28.210 --> 00:34:31.210
Wherever there's power, there'll be men like Lex to exploit it.

00:34:31.210 --> 00:34:35.210
Maybe you can do something, maybe open an investigation.

00:34:35.210 --> 00:34:40.210
Clark, I'm a little fish in a tiny pond. My influence doesn't reach nearly that far up.

00:34:40.210 --> 00:34:43.210
And perhaps it's time to extend that influence.

00:34:43.210 --> 00:34:48.289
I just got off the phone with the governor.

00:34:48.289 --> 00:34:52.289
We were talking about your filling Burke's senatorial seat until the next election.

00:34:52.289 --> 00:34:53.289
the next election.

00:34:53.289 --> 00:34:54.289
Me?

00:34:54.289 --> 00:34:58.289
Kansas needs to be represented by someone of unassailable character

00:34:58.289 --> 00:35:02.289
who can restore the faith that Burke has tarnished.

00:35:02.289 --> 00:35:07.289
The governor agreed you are the perfect choice for the U.S. Senate.

00:35:07.289 --> 00:35:14.110
You agree?

00:35:14.110 --> 00:35:30.500
I think you should do it.

00:35:30.500 --> 00:35:34.389
I think Dad would have wanted you to.

00:35:34.389 --> 00:35:38.980
I can't move to Washington.

00:35:38.980 --> 00:35:41.980
We're barely keeping the farm running as it is.

00:35:41.980 --> 00:35:49.210
Oh, Clark can take care of that, can't you, Clark?

00:35:49.210 --> 00:35:51.210
I could lease out the back forter to Ben Hubbard.

00:35:51.210 --> 00:35:53.210
He's been wanting to work that land for years.

00:35:53.210 --> 00:35:56.670
Oh, Clark.

00:35:56.670 --> 00:36:00.980
You and Dad always taught me to put other people first.

00:36:00.980 --> 00:36:05.460
To use my abilities to help those in need.

00:36:05.460 --> 00:36:08.460
You have the chance to affect so many people,

00:36:08.460 --> 00:36:11.460
to change so many lives if you go to Washington.

00:36:11.460 --> 00:36:16.340
It's where you need to be if you really want to make a difference, Mom.

00:36:16.340 --> 00:36:22.309
And it's where people like West need you to be.

00:36:22.309 --> 00:36:36.570
I don't care what it takes.

00:36:36.570 --> 00:36:39.570
I want the body transported to the lab immediately.

00:36:39.570 --> 00:36:44.769
Make it happen.

00:36:44.769 --> 00:36:46.769
Hey, you're up.

00:36:46.769 --> 00:36:47.769
For a while now.

00:36:47.769 --> 00:36:50.769
You never came home last night.

00:36:50.769 --> 00:36:53.769
There was an unforeseen complication with Project Aries.

00:36:53.769 --> 00:36:55.769
Aries?

00:36:55.769 --> 00:36:59.769
The secret military project I was discussing with Senator Burke yesterday.

00:36:59.769 --> 00:37:03.940
When you were listening outside the door...

00:37:03.940 --> 00:37:12.059
Lex, I'm sorry.

00:37:12.059 --> 00:37:15.300
There is no excuse.

00:37:15.300 --> 00:37:17.300
My curiosity got the best of me.

00:37:17.300 --> 00:37:23.150
You're not a cat, Lana.

00:37:23.150 --> 00:37:25.150
Don't skulk around like one.

00:37:25.150 --> 00:37:46.960
I'm very disappointed.

00:37:46.960 --> 00:38:11.210
If you ever betrayed me, my business dealings.

00:38:11.210 --> 00:38:14.579
To ask.

00:38:16.239 --> 00:38:17.239
No secrets.

00:38:17.239 --> 00:38:32.420
Mrs. Kent goes to Washington.

00:38:32.420 --> 00:38:36.420
Well, if anyone can give Jimmy Stewart a run for his money...

00:38:36.420 --> 00:38:38.420
I just wish Lionel wasn't helping her.

00:38:38.420 --> 00:38:41.420
But you think the king of ulterior motives may have something up his Armani's sleeve?

00:38:41.420 --> 00:38:45.420
When doesn't he? Just right now, his son's a bigger problem.

00:38:45.420 --> 00:38:48.420
That's a understatement of the century.

00:38:48.420 --> 00:38:51.420
I mean, we've always known Lex as a dark side, but with what he's been doing recently,

00:38:51.420 --> 00:38:53.420
we're headed towards pitch black.

00:38:53.420 --> 00:38:56.420
I want to make sure that Lana's nowhere near him when the lights go out.

00:38:56.420 --> 00:38:57.420
Well, hopefully he'll be behind bars long before.

00:38:57.420 --> 00:39:00.420
bars long before that. I mean, Lois is meeting the feds at the morgue.

00:39:00.420 --> 00:39:04.420
And once they connect Wes's body with Lex and then Burke's murder...

00:39:04.420 --> 00:39:06.420
Don't hold your breath.

00:39:06.420 --> 00:39:08.420
Wes's body's gone.

00:39:08.420 --> 00:39:12.420
What about the feds? I mean, what did they say when you told them what happened?

00:39:12.420 --> 00:39:16.420
I work at the Inquisitor. You know, aliens, Bigfoot, Elvis, what do you think they said?

00:39:16.420 --> 00:39:21.420
As far as they're concerned, Wes Keenan died in action four months ago.

00:39:21.420 --> 00:39:24.420
Just like it said in his file.

00:39:24.420 --> 00:39:26.420
He deserved better than this.

00:39:27.420 --> 00:39:29.420
I'm sorry.

00:39:29.420 --> 00:39:31.420
Don't be sorry for me.

00:39:31.420 --> 00:39:33.420
Be sorry for Lex.

00:39:33.420 --> 00:39:36.420
He's going to pay for what he did to Wes.

00:39:36.420 --> 00:39:39.420
And I'm going to make damn sure that he doesn't do this to anyone else.

00:39:39.420 --> 00:40:05.969
Take him apart.

00:40:05.969 --> 00:40:09.969
I want to know exactly what went wrong so we don't make the same mistake next time.

00:40:09.969 --> 00:40:13.969
Quantitating the abnormality won't do us any good, Mr. Luther.

00:40:13.969 --> 00:40:17.969
We used up nearly everything we harvested from Titan.

00:40:17.969 --> 00:40:20.969
There aren't enough alien peptide sequences to continue the project.

00:40:20.969 --> 00:40:24.969
I'm already working on procuring a replacement.

00:40:24.969 --> 00:40:31.889
I promise you, Doctor, this isn't the end of Project Aries.

00:40:31.889 --> 00:40:37.219
This is just the beginning.

